  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-25$v$, $v$Textured Turquoise$v$, $v$amaco-textured-turquoise$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$A subtle turquoise gloss, green-beige where thin, but a beautiful aqua where thick$v$, $v$#95af8f$v$, $v$turquoise$v$, array[$v$turquoise$v$,$v$green$v$,$v$beige$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$A subtle turquoise gloss, green-beige where thin, but a beautiful aqua where thick. Great for textured ware and layering with other Potter's Choice glazes. It is a fluid glaze.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-25-textured-turquoise/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/464/images/2671/PC-25_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__43675.1659532451.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-26$v$, $v$Blue Lagoon$v$, $v$amaco-blue-lagoon$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$The cool tones of Blue Lagoon break milky green and pool into light blue shallows when applied over deep texture$v$, $v$#9db7b3$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$The cool tones of Blue Lagoon break milky green and pool into light blue shallows when applied over deep texture. When heavier coats are applied this allows the glaze to float up and create interesting surface variations similar to tides in a blue lagoon. A fluid glaze.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-26-blue-lagoon/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/2092/images/3270/PC-26_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__00493.1663168137.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-27$v$, $v$Tourmaline$v$, $v$amaco-tourmaline$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Tourmaline is an intense, opaque blue-green glaze that forms a smooth, strong surface$v$, $v$#557669$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], null, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Tourmaline is an intense, opaque blue-green glaze that forms a smooth, strong surface. Goes well layered with other potters choice glazes!$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-27-tourmaline/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/465/images/2669/PC-27_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__16243.1659532378.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-28$v$, $v$Frosted Turquoise$v$, $v$amaco-frosted-turquoise$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Frosted Turquoise is an opaque gray-blue glaze that appears to crackle over deep blue but has a smooth, satiny surface$v$, $v$#8a9b95$v$, $v$turquoise$v$, array[$v$turquoise$v$,$v$gray$v$,$v$blue$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Frosted Turquoise is an opaque gray-blue glaze that appears to crackle over deep blue but has a smooth, satiny surface. This glaze is a great, detailed surface decoration for subtle, simple forms. Frosted Turquoise benefits from a heavy application to achieve its color breaking effect. The glaze color is susceptible to variation due to iron fuming from nearby pots in firing.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-28-frosted-turquoise/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/466/images/2667/PC-28_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__76599.1659532264.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-29$v$, $v$Deep Olive Speckle$v$, $v$amaco-deep-olive-speckle$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Deep Olive Speckle is a rich, translucent, glossy green glaze with darker green speckles$v$, $v$#968b3b$v$, $v$olive$v$, array[$v$olive$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Deep Olive Speckle is a rich, translucent, glossy green glaze with darker green speckles. Looks great when layered with our other Potter's Choice glazes. This glaze contains black speckles that may clog a spray gun. Make sure glaze is well-mixed for even distribution of speckles.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-29-deep-olive-speckle/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/467/images/2665/PC-29_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__45333.1659532134.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-30$v$, $v$Temmoku$v$, $v$amaco-temmoku$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Temmoku is a textured, satin-matte dark brown/tan speckled glaze that looks great layered beneath some of the more fluid Potter's Choice gla$v$, $v$#6b5432$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$,$v$tan$v$]::text[], $v$satin$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Temmoku is a textured, satin-matte dark brown/tan speckled glaze that looks great layered beneath some of the more fluid Potter's Choice glazes. With its consistent surface and reliable results, this glaze makes a fantastic liner for cups, pots, bowls, and other ware.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-30-temmoku/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/468/images/2664/PC-30_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__04587.1659532041.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-31$v$, $v$Oatmeal$v$, $v$amaco-oatmeal$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Oatmeal is a toasty, light beige glaze that is relatively translucent and breaks clear over textured surfaces$v$, $v$#d8c275$v$, $v$beige$v$, array[$v$beige$v$,$v$clear$v$]::text[], null, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Oatmeal is a toasty, light beige glaze that is relatively translucent and breaks clear over textured surfaces. This glaze is great for layering with other Potters Choice glazes. Try layered over PC-33 Iron Lustre!$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-31-oatmeal/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/454/images/2694/PC-31_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__71374.1659533730.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-32$v$, $v$Albany Slip Brown$v$, $v$amaco-albany-slip-brown$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Like the traditional potter's glaze that inspired it, Albany Slip Brown is fluid and butter colored where thick and russet where thin$v$, $v$#a16238$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Like the traditional potter's glaze that inspired it, Albany Slip Brown is fluid and butter colored where thick and russet where thin. Great layered over or under other Potter's Choice glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-32-albany-slip-brown/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/469/images/2660/PC-32_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__89484.1659531904.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-33$v$, $v$Iron Lustre$v$, $v$amaco-iron-lustre$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$More restrained, but similar to a regular blue glaze, Iron Lustre is brown where thin with blue-gray floats where thick$v$, $v$#645640$v$, $v$blue$v$, array[$v$blue$v$,$v$brown$v$,$v$gray$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$More restrained, but similar to a regular blue glaze, Iron Lustre is brown where thin with blue-gray floats where thick. It is beautiful on texture and layers well with other Potter's Choice glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-33-iron-lustre/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/470/images/2658/PC-33_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__61306.1659531820.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-34$v$, $v$Light Sepia$v$, $v$amaco-light-sepia$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Light Sepia is an opalescent grey glaze that features strong variations on textured ware$v$, $v$#a9a086$v$, $v$gray$v$, array[$v$gray$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Light Sepia is an opalescent grey glaze that features strong variations on textured ware. This glaze breaks golden beige where thin and lends well to layering with our other Potters Choice Glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-34-light-sepia/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/471/images/2657/PC-34_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__84472.1659531661.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-36$v$, $v$Ironstone$v$, $v$amaco-ironstone$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Ironstone is a glossy, dark glaze that is a deep chocolatey brown where thin with a beige-bronze float where thicker$v$, $v$#4d4a33$v$, $v$brown$v$, array[$v$brown$v$,$v$beige$v$,$v$bronze$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Ironstone is a glossy, dark glaze that is a deep chocolatey brown where thin with a beige-bronze float where thicker. Mixes well with other Potter's Choice Glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-36-ironstone/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/473/images/2651/PC-36_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__48479.1659531409.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-38$v$, $v$Iron Yellow$v$, $v$amaco-iron-yellow$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Iron Yellow is a glossy, soft yellow glaze with flecks of iron, that is relatively opaque and breaks clear over texture$v$, $v$#a69b79$v$, $v$yellow$v$, array[$v$yellow$v$,$v$clear$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Iron Yellow is a glossy, soft yellow glaze with flecks of iron, that is relatively opaque and breaks clear over texture. Excellent as a liner glaze for pots where the goal is to show off the decorations on the outside of the vessel.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-38-iron-yellow/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/2093/images/3271/PC-38_Iron_Yellow__39409.1663168567.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-40$v$, $v$True Celadon$v$, $v$amaco-true-celadon$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$True Celadon is a delicate light green glaze that reproduces the effects of traditional Asian celadons$v$, $v$#a4b370$v$, $v$celadon$v$, array[$v$celadon$v$,$v$green$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$True Celadon is a delicate light green glaze that reproduces the effects of traditional Asian celadons. This glaze looks striking over any textured ware and has great color response when layered with our other Potter's Choice glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-40-true-celadon/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/477/images/2644/PC-40_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__79878.1659465592.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-41$v$, $v$Vert Lustre$v$, $v$amaco-vert-lustre$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Vert Lustre is a beautiful flowing green glaze with a metallic sheen like that of ancient Persian Lusterware$v$, $v$#738356$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Vert Lustre is a beautiful flowing green glaze with a metallic sheen like that of ancient Persian Lusterware. This glaze reacts well to texture and has great effects when layered with other Potter's Choice Glazes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-41-vert-lustre/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/478/images/2642/PC-41_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__41955.1659465323.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-42$v$, $v$Seaweed$v$, $v$amaco-seaweed$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Seaweed is a fluid, deep green glaze that layers beautifully with a variety of Potter's Choice glazes$v$, $v$#4c4a25$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Seaweed is a fluid, deep green glaze that layers beautifully with a variety of Potter's Choice glazes. This glaze breaks brownish over texture and becomes more fluid with thickness. Pay attention to application thickness so the glaze does not flow onto kiln shelves during firing.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-42-seaweed/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/479/images/2640/PC-42_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__74984.1659465238.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
