  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-47$v$, $v$Emerald Falls$v$, $v$amaco-emerald-falls$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Emerald Falls is a beautiful glossy green glaze that breaks lighter and pools into a mauve grey-green$v$, $v$#83937b$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$gray$v$]::text[], $v$gloss$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Emerald Falls is a beautiful glossy green glaze that breaks lighter and pools into a mauve grey-green. When heavier coats are applied this allows the glaze to float up and create interesting surface variations echoing mossy patches found in rolling emerald landscapes.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-47-emerald-falls/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/2094/images/3272/PC-47_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__26762.1663168805.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-48$v$, $v$Art Deco Green$v$, $v$amaco-art-deco-green$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Art Deco Green is a glossy, light blue-green glaze that floats metallic spots to the surface resembling a patinate copper roof$v$, $v$#65664c$v$, $v$green$v$, array[$v$green$v$,$v$blue$v$,$v$bronze$v$]::text[], $v$metallic$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Art Deco Green is a glossy, light blue-green glaze that floats metallic spots to the surface resembling a patinate copper roof.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-48-art-deco-green/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/482/images/2634/PC-48_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__30933.1659464921.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-49$v$, $v$Frosted Melon$v$, $v$amaco-frosted-melon$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Frosted Melon is a very unique glaze with some qualities that can be exploited for additional interest$v$, $v$#bec9a2$v$, null, '{}'::text[], $v$satin$v$, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Frosted Melon is a very unique glaze with some qualities that can be exploited for additional interest. It has a massive, beige float with heavy application. This float "cracks", showing the green of the glaze below while still maintaining a smooth, satin surface. This subtle glaze is beautiful on smooth and textured ware alike.The glaze color is susceptible to variation due to iron fuming from other pots nearby in firing.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-49-frosted-melon/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/483/images/2630/PC-49_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__57487.1659464753.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-52$v$, $v$Deep Sienna Speckle$v$, $v$amaco-deep-sienna-speckle$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Deep Sienna Speckle is a warm, rich russet glaze that is translucent with dark speckles that resemble the surface of reduction stoneware gla$v$, $v$#8f4121$v$, null, '{}'::text[], null, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Deep Sienna Speckle is a warm, rich russet glaze that is translucent with dark speckles that resemble the surface of reduction stoneware glazes. For more depth and concentration of color, apply thicker. This glaze layers well with our other Potter's Choice glazes. This glaze contains black speckles, so make sure glaze is mixed well to assure they are well dispersed. Specks may clog spray gun.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-52-deep-sienna-speckle/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/485/images/2627/PC-52_6x6_Lablel_Tile_Chip-hires__56119.1659464566.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-53$v$, $v$Ancient Jasper$v$, $v$amaco-ancient-jasper$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Ancient Jasper is a fluid, opaque glaze that transitions from soft black to olive green to rust red as it is applied thicker$v$, $v$#53432f$v$, $v$black$v$, array[$v$black$v$,$v$olive$v$,$v$green$v$,$v$rust$v$,$v$red$v$]::text[], null, $v$opaque$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Ancient Jasper is a fluid, opaque glaze that transitions from soft black to olive green to rust red as it is applied thicker. This glaze has an active, varied surface by itself and layers with our other Potter's Choice glazes with striking results.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-53-ancient-jasper/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/486/images/2626/PC-53_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__26696.1659464448.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-55$v$, $v$Chun Plum$v$, $v$amaco-chun-plum$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Chun Plum is a pink-red translucent glaze that breaks light tan over textures$v$, $v$#713f41$v$, $v$plum$v$, array[$v$plum$v$,$v$pink$v$,$v$red$v$,$v$tan$v$]::text[], null, $v$translucent$v$, 5, 6, null, $v$Chun Plum is a pink-red translucent glaze that breaks light tan over textures. This glaze imitates the copper reds of Asia but with a reliable color response in oxidation firings. Layer over other Potters Choice glazes for a warmer tone and hints of pink and red.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-55-chun-plum/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/487/images/2623/PC-55_6x6_Label_Tile_Chip-hires__83382.1659464356.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
  ($v$amaco$v$, $v$potters-choice$v$, $v$PC-56$v$, $v$Ancient Copper$v$, $v$amaco-ancient-copper$v$, $v$glaze$v$, $v$Inspired by classic tomato red reduction glazes, Ancient Copper is an iridescent, iron red glaze that breaks dark brown over texture and poo$v$, $v$#a97977$v$, $v$bronze$v$, array[$v$bronze$v$,$v$red$v$,$v$brown$v$]::text[], null, null, 5, 6, null, $v$Inspired by classic tomato red reduction glazes, Ancient Copper is an iridescent, iron red glaze that breaks dark brown over texture and pools dark yellow-green, giving it a weathered appearance.$v$, $v$https://shop.amaco.com/pc-56-ancient-copper/$v$, $v$AMACO: optimal results at Cone 5/6 (Cone 5 = 1186 °C, Cone 6 = 1222 °C). Apply to bisqueware fired to Cone 04 (1063 °C). Source: https://shop.amaco.com/glazes-underglazes/high-fire-glazes/pc-potters-choice/$v$, null, null, $v$https://cdn11.bigcommerce.com/s-a0h9fhqogk/products/2326/images/3786/PC-56_Cone5_TileA_WEB__72288.1714744727.386.513.jpg?c=1$v$, $v$AMACO$v$),
